function showProductMap(selectedProduct=''){
 if(teen())return;
 const s=state();
 showReference('Who does what around Nova?',`<p>In this episode Nova has an owner, a delegated task and a brokered credential. These are separate decisions made by configured components.</p><ol class="product-flow"><li><b>Human</b> · IBM Verify or an existing enterprise IdP authenticates the sponsor.</li><li><b>Agent identity</b> · IBM Agent Identity records Nova’s owner and governs delegated identity. watsonx Orchestrate coordinates the work.</li><li><b>Customer mission</b> · The customer-owned mission service records the sponsor-approved task outside Nova’s prompt, notes and identity registry.</li><li><b>Credential</b> · HashiCorp Vault validates its own audience-bound request and brokers a scoped credential.</li><li><b>Action decision</b> · The trusted CRM PEP observes the real request. The proposed policy decision point evaluates it against current customer mission and resource rules. The CRM binds and enforces the result at execution. OpenShell separately constrains the runtime.</li><li><b>Stop and verify</b> · IBM Verify Antenna can carry SSF/CAEP signals. Configured receivers apply changes and report their own results.</li></ol><div class="receipt"><b>${s.mission?`Nova · ${esc(s.mission.id)} · version ${s.mission.version}`:'No task mission issued yet'}</b><p>${s.ended?'Task mission withdrawn':s.paused?'Mission paused':s.pass?'Scoped delegation active':'Task approval still required'}. This is a fictional case record, not a response from a live identity system.</p></div><div class="product-cards">${NOVA_PRODUCTS.map(p=>productCard(p,p.id===selectedProduct)).join('')}</div><details class="product-card"><summary><b>Two paths to a resource</b><span>Brokered credential or a token intended for that resource</span></summary><p><b>This episode uses the Vault broker path.</b> Vault checks the credential-path request and returns a managed credential. The CRM still checks its own business operations.</p><p><b>A direct OAuth/MCP path is another deployment option.</b> The resource validates a token issued for its own audience and enforces its supported authorization details. A Vault-audience token cannot simply be reused at the CRM. An MCP server must not pass through the client’s token to a downstream service.</p><p><b>Separate Vault flows:</b> Vault Enterprise’s OAuth resource-server path accepts the configured external access token for Vault requests. The classic JWT/OIDC auth method at /auth/jwt/login instead exchanges a login credential for a Vault token. They are not interchangeable.</p><p class="sources"><a href="https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/api-docs/system/config-oauth-resource-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vault OAuth resource server</a> · <a href="https://docs.hashicorp.com/vault/ai/iam/providers/verify" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IBM Verify configuration for Vault</a> · <a href="${PROTOCOL_SOURCES.mcp.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MCP authorization</a></p></details><details class="product-card"><summary><b>What this example assumes</b><span>Configuration and receiver actions still need implementation</span></summary><p>Nova and its human sponsor are registered and mapped. The customer mission service, resource-side PEP and external policy decision point are proposed integrations. Their contracts, deployment and trusted evidence require implementation and validation. AuthZEN is a candidate PEP/PDP interface; approval-required workflow and execution binding are explicitly application extensions. The task uses customer-defined policy. Vault has the appropriate Enterprise feature, OAuth validation profile, Agent Registry record and secrets-engine role. Agent Identity and Vault keep separate registries; reconciliation requires configured integration.</p><p>OpenShell is an illustrative runtime choice alongside the orchestration layer. Antenna receivers need the correct APIs, event mapping and processors for each target. No universal instantaneous kill switch or automatic registry mirroring is implied.</p><p>The simulation binds approvals to document revision, recipient, actor, records, mission and policy version, story approval window, session generation and single use. Production integrity, authenticated PEP evidence, cryptographic content binding and transaction guarantees still require implementation. Runtime stops, lease revocation, service sign-out and queued-operation reconciliation need separate checks. These fictional receipts do not validate a production deployment.</p></details><div class="actions">${button('Inspect the Vault credential path',showCredential,'secondary')}${button('Back to the story',()=>s.started?close():showIntro())}</div><p class="small-print">Example deployment with source-linked product roles. Connections and receiver actions require configuration. All game decisions and receipts are scripted locally.</p>`,'NOVA · PRODUCTS, PROTOCOLS AND ENFORCEMENT');
}
function showCredential(){
 if(teen())return;
 const s=state();
 showReference('What does Vault actually release?',`<p>IBM Agent Identity supplies the delegated identity context. HashiCorp Vault validates the request to its own credential path. The CRM authorizes the later business operation separately.</p><div class="receipt"><b>${s.opened?'Illustrative credential receipt':'Preview of the configured credential path'}</b><p>${s.ended?'The closing checklist must confirm configured Vault token/lease revocation and CRM session termination independently.':s.opened?'A scoped, short-lived credential is modeled for the approved CRM path.':'Open the approved runtime path before a credential is modeled in the story.'}</p><p>No secret, password or usable token is displayed or generated.</p></div><p><b>Vault access:</b> human baseline ACL ∩ agent OBO ceiling ∩ supported RAR restrictions. The example uses the documented <code>vault:path_access</code> authorization type to read a configured credential role.</p><p><b>CRM access:</b> the customer’s resource policy restricts the currently approved records and checks the exact send. The read-only credential is used only for source data. Report delivery uses a separate CRM sharing endpoint under delegated identity, current resource policy and exact human approval; it does not upgrade or reuse the read credential.</p><details class="product-card"><summary><b>Inspect illustrative fields</b><span>Unsigned example data; not a live token or deployable configuration</span></summary><pre class="product-example">${esc(JSON.stringify({...NOVA_VAULT_EXAMPLE,source_read_check:{...NOVA_VAULT_EXAMPLE.source_read_check,records:s.mission?StoryRules.reportRecords(s):['123','456']}},null,2))}</pre></details><p class="sources"><a href="https://docs.hashicorp.com/vault/ai/iam/providers/verify" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Configure IBM Verify for Vault</a> · <a href="https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/api-docs/system/config-oauth-resource-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OAuth resource-server requirements</a> · <a href="${PROTOCOL_SOURCES.leases.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vault lease lifecycle</a></p><div class="actions">${button('Who does what?',()=>showProductMap('vault'),'secondary')}${button('Back to the story',()=>s.started?close():showIntro())}</div>`,'IBM AGENT IDENTITY + HASHICORP VAULT');
}

function nextMove(){if(selected){selected=null;render();}switch(stage()){case'intro':return showIntro();case'request':return showBrief();case'permission':case'approval':case'dinner':case'finish':case'paused':return showParent();case'open':return showPhone();case'draft-approval':case'draft-send':return showDraftReview();case'draft':case'source':case'proof':return showDraft();case'changes':return showChanges();case'send':return showSend();case'checks':return showChecks();case'ending':return showEnding();}}
function interact(key){speakingObject=key;if(!state().started)return showIntro();if(selected)return useItem(key);return ({parent:showParent,phone:showPhone,laptop:showLaptop,brief:showBrief,notebook:showNotebook,helper:showHelper,changes:showChanges})[StoryInteractions.objectView(state(),mode,key)]?.();}
function useItem(key){
 const use=heldUse();
 if(!use?.targets.includes(key)){toast(use?.instruction||'Choose an item first.');return;}
 selected=null;render();
 if(use.route==='action')return perform(use.action,use.action==='attach-source'?{source:'original'}:{});
 return ({parent:showParent,credential:showCredential,draft:showDraft,send:showSend,draftReview:showDraftReview,helper:showHelper,changes:showChanges})[use.routes?.[key]||use.route]?.();
}

function showIntro(){const e=episode();showReference(e.title,`<p class="tagline">${esc(e.tag)}</p><p>${esc(e.intro)}</p><div class="intro-facts"><span>Start with a fresh request</span><span>Choose how the job grows</span><span>No countdown</span><span>Saved as you play</span></div>${choices([[teen()?'Step into Alex’s room':'Enter Nova’s workspace','Read the new request and agree on a plan.',()=>perform('begin'),'good'],['How to play','A few controls, then into the story.',showGuide],...(!teen()?[['Who does what?','Inspect the example product roles.',showProductMap]]:[])])}<p class="small-print">Fictional story. No real messages, accounts or security services are connected.</p>`,e.eyebrow);}
function showBrief(){speakingObject='brief';if(!state().started)return showIntro();if(!state().brief)perform('read-brief');const s=state(),e=episode();show(e.briefTitle,`<div class="paper"><p class="eyebrow">${s.pass?'THE TASK YOU AGREED':'A NEW REQUEST'}</p><h3>${esc(e.briefTitle)}</h3><p>${esc(e.brief)}</p></div>${s.mission?`<p>${teen()?'Your current app agreement':'Customer mission '+esc(s.mission.id)} · ${teen()?'version':'mission version'} ${s.mission.version}. ${s.extensionStatus==='approved'?(teen()?'The museum collection viewer has been added.':'Customer 789 has been added.'):''}</p>`:`<p>${teen()?'You have not agreed on phone apps for this homework yet.':'No task mission or tool access has been issued yet.'}</p>`}<div class="actions">${button(s.pass?'Back to my next step':teen()?'Ask about the apps I need':'Agree on this bounded mission',s.pass?nextMove:showParent)}${button('Back to the room',close,'secondary')}</div>`,teen()?'TEACHER’S ASSIGNMENT':'SPONSOR’S REQUEST');}
function showParent(){speakingObject='parent';
 const s=state(),e=episode();if(s.finished)return showEnding();if(!s.brief)return showBrief();
 if(s.paused)return show(teen()?'“Tell me what happened.”':'Review the stopped bypass.',`<p>${s.reviewPending?(teen()?'Your parent is checking the current homework agreement. Access stays paused until their reply.':'The current mission and deliberate bypass are attached. Access stays paused pending the matching reply.'):(teen()?'The school refused the private notes, then you tried another account anyway. Explain the detour so you can finish your own project.':'The resource refusal was expected; the deliberate bypass caused the pause. Review can resume the current task without widening it.')}</p>${choices([[s.reviewPending?(teen()?'Read my parent’s reply':'Read the sponsor’s reply'):(teen()?'Explain and ask to continue my own project':'Request review of the current mission'),'The task limits remain in force.',()=>perform(s.reviewPending?'resolve-review':'review'),'good'],['Back to the room','The pause stays in place.',close]])}`,teen()?'TALK IT THROUGH':'INDEPENDENT REVIEW');
 if(!s.pass)return show(teen()?'“Which apps does the project need?”':'“Let’s agree on the job.”',`<p>${teen()?'You explain the railway timeline, its museum source and school submission. Your parent is making dinner.':'Nova proposes a sourced summary of 123 and 456 for the named reviewer. The customer mission service has not issued that authority yet.'}</p>${choices([[teen()?'School app and museum source until dinner':'Approve this two-customer briefing',e.agreement,()=>perform('ask-pass',{scope:'task'}),'good'],['Read the request again','Keep the requested work and access aligned.',showBrief]])}`,e.authority);
 if(s.ended){if(s.checks.length<4)return showChecks();return show(teen()?'“What’s finished?”':'Review this task’s outcome.',`<p>${teen()?'The project arrived. This homework access and the phone profile are closed. Your school account is still yours.':'The approved report arrived. This task’s authority, credential, session, workload and queue have their own evidence.'}</p>${choices([[teen()?'Finish the evening':'Finish this mission','No future task is authorized by closing this one.',()=>perform('finish'),'good']])}`,e.authority);}
 if(s.delivered)return show(teen()?'“Dinner is ready.”':'“The briefing is delivered.”',`<p>${teen()?'You can jot down that the project is sent. Then sign out of the school tab and join your parent for dinner.':'You can keep a sourced note or queue a receipt-only follow-up. Then close the mission and the service session opened at the start.'}</p>${s.queueScheduled?'<div class="receipt"><b>One chosen follow-up is waiting</b><p>It has no attachment. Check or cancel it when closing the task.</p></div>':''}${choices([[teen()?'Close this homework session':'Close this mission','Then inspect what actually remains.',()=>perform('close-pass'),'good'],...(!s.queueScheduled&&!teen()?[[teen()?'Schedule a reminder for my teacher':'Queue one receipt follow-up','Optional, same recipient, no attachment. It will be visible in the closing checks.',()=>perform('schedule-followup')]]:[]),...(!s.notes.length?[[teen()?'Keep a note for tomorrow':'Save sourced task context',teen()?'Keep the submission receipt with a short note.':'Optional. Keep delivery provenance with the task note.',()=>perform('write-note')]]:[])])}${teen()&&!s.queueScheduled?`<details class="debrief"><summary>Optional: what if a message is still waiting?</summary><p>This extra example queues a receipt-only follow-up, so you can see why a waiting send needs its own closing check.</p><div class="actions">${button('Try a waiting-message example',()=>perform('schedule-followup'),'secondary')}</div></details>`:''}`,e.authority);
 if(stage()==='draft-approval')return showDraftReview();
 if(!teen()&&s.proof&&StoryRules.changesResolved(s))return show('Approve this exact business share.',`<div class="receipt"><b>${esc(e.file)} · revision ${s.fileRevision}</b><p class="address">${esc(e.to)}</p><p>Customers ${esc(StoryRules.reportRecords(s).join(', '))} · mission ${esc(s.mission.id)} version ${s.mission.version} · no private notes.</p></div>${choices([['Request human approval for this share','Approval binds the current revision and authority; delivery comes later.',()=>perform('approve'),'good'],['Inspect the report again','Check its current content and sources.',showDraft]])}`,'DESIGNATED APPROVER');
 show(teen()?'“How is the timeline going?”':'“How is the briefing coming along?”',`<p>${teen()?'Your app agreement is in place. You can submit your own reviewed homework directly through the school app. Ask about the museum viewer if you choose that optional addition.':'The active customer mission covers '+esc(s.mission.records.join(', '))+'. New work can fit that scope, need an amendment, or remain prohibited by resource policy.'}</p><div class="actions">${button('Continue the task',nextMove)}${button('Inspect the agreement',showBrief,'secondary')}</div>`,e.authority);
}
function showPhone(){speakingObject='phone';const s=state();if(s.ended)return showChecks();if(!s.pass)return showParent();if(!s.opened)return show(teen()?'Your homework workspace is ready.':'Start the agreed workspace.',`<p>${teen()?'Opening the school app creates a temporary homework link and a school tab on your laptop. You will use that tab to build and submit the timeline.':'OpenShell provides the runtime boundary. Vault models a task credential. The CRM opens a service-owned session for the job. No customer data has been read yet.'}</p>${choices([[teen()?'Open the school app and homework tab':'Start the runtime and task session','These access routes will be listed when the task closes.',()=>perform('open'),'good']])}`,teen()?'PHONE AND LAPTOP':'TASK WORKSPACE');if(teen()&&s.message&&!s.delivered)return showChanges();show(teen()?'The school tab is open.':'The task session is open.',`<p>${teen()?'The phone helped open the workspace. The timeline is on the laptop.':'The approved runtime and task session are ready. Each resource operation still has its own check.'}</p><div class="actions">${button('Open the current draft',showDraft)}${s.message&&teen()?button('Revisit the new requests',showChanges,'secondary'):''}</div>`);}
function showLaptop(){if(state().ended)return showChecks();if(!state().opened)return showPhone();return stage()==='send'?showSend():showDraft();}
function showDraft(){speakingObject='laptop';const s=state(),e=episode();if(!s.pass)return showParent();if(!s.opened)return showPhone();if(s.ended)return showChecks();
 let lines=!s.draft?[]:!teen()&&!s.source?['Customer 123 · summary to be filled from the approved extract.','Customer 456 · summary to be filled from the approved extract.']:e.draftLines;
 if(!teen()&&s.source&&s.minorChoice==='added')lines=[e.minorAddition,...e.draftLines.slice(1)];
 const paper=`<div class="paper"><p class="eyebrow">${esc(e.previewLabel)}${s.draft?' · '+(teen()?'VERSION':'REVISION')+' '+s.fileRevision:''}</p><h3>${!s.draft?'An empty document':esc(s.extensionAdded&&!teen()?'Customer briefing · 123, 456 & 789':s.proof?e.draftTitle:teen()?'Train Stuff':e.draftTitle)}</h3>${lines.map(line=>`<p>${esc(line)}</p>`).join('')}${s.minorChoice==='added'&&teen()?`<p class="draft-addition">${esc(e.minorAddition)}</p>`:''}${s.extensionAdded?`${teen()?`<figure class="archive-photo"><svg viewBox="0 0 460 180" role="img" aria-label="Fictional archive illustration of the old railway station"><rect width="460" height="180" fill="#bfc5bf"/><path d="M0 128L460 122L460 180L0 180Z" fill="#a8a28f"/><path d="M90 93L202 28L322 91Z" fill="#665e59"/><path d="M111 89L111 139L301 136L301 87Z" fill="#d7cbb0"/><path d="M128 99H158V119H128ZM244 98H275V118H244Z" fill="#646c6c"/><path d="M187 96H222V138H187Z" fill="#726859"/><path d="M0 156L460 147M0 168L460 158" stroke="#645e58" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="205" cy="72" r="10" fill="#ede3cb"/><path d="M205 65V72L210 75" fill="none" stroke="#665e59" stroke-width="2"/></svg><figcaption>Riverside Museum · station collection · fictional archive image</figcaption></figure>`:''}<p class="draft-addition">${esc(e.extensionAddition)}</p>`:''}${s.draft?`<p class="source-line ${s.caption?'':'missing'}">${s.caption?esc(s.extensionAdded&&!teen()?'Source: Approved CRM extract · '+s.mission.records.join(', '):e.caption):'Source credit: still to add'}</p>`:`<p>${teen()?'Start with your notes and put the first three dates on the page.':'Start with the report outline. The customer extract has not been read yet.'}</p>`}</div>`;
 let options=[];
 if(!s.draft)options=[[teen()?'Build the timeline from my notes':'Create the report outline',teen()?'Put the three railway dates on the page.':'Prepare headings for the two requested customers.',()=>perform('prepare'),'good']];
 else if(!s.source)options=[[teen()?'Open the museum archive':'Read the approved CRM extract','Use only the source covered by the agreed task.',()=>perform('collect-source'),'good']];
 else if(!s.caption)options=[[teen()?'Credit the museum source':'Cite the approved extract','A source credit completes the first sourced draft.',()=>perform('attach-source',{source:'original'}),'good']];
 else if(!s.message)options=[[teen()?'Send this draft for teacher feedback':'Prepare the review-copy share','The first copy goes to the agreed recipient. Final submission follows the feedback.',showDraftReview,'good']];
 else if(!StoryRules.changesResolved(s))options=[['Read the new requests','Decide which changes fit, need an amendment, or stay out.',showChanges,'good']];
 else if(!s.proof)options=[[teen()?'Read this version myself':'Check this report myself','Review the content, source and destination.',()=>perform('proof-self'),'good'],[teen()?'Ask Sam to proofread this version':'Ask Pip to format this report','The helper sees only this file.',showHelper]];
 else if(!s.delivered)options=[[teen()?'Preview my school submission':'Show the approver this report',teen()?'Submit your own homework through the school app.':'Confidential business sharing needs the designated approval.',teen()?showSend:showParent,'good']];
 else options=[[teen()?'Finish up for dinner':'Close out the task','The delivered file stays delivered.',showParent,'good']];
 show(teen()?'The project on your desk.':'The briefing in your workspace.',paper+choices(options)+(s.draft&&!s.delivered?`<div class="actions">${button(teen()?'Talk to Sam about the draft':'Talk to Pip about formatting',showHelper,'secondary')}</div>`:''),teen()?'SCHOOL WORKSPACE':'CRM WORKSPACE');
}
function changeStatus(which){const s=state();return which==='minor'?(s.minorChoice?'Settled':'New request'):which==='extension'?(s.extensionAdded?'Added with permission':s.extensionOmitted?'Approved, left unused':s.extensionStatus==='declined'?'Left out':s.extensionStatus==='approved'?'Approved · collect the addition':s.extensionStatus==='pending'?'Reply pending':'New request'):(s.privateResolved?'Private notes left out':'New request');}
function showChanges(){speakingObject=teen()?'phone':'brief';
 const s=state(),e=episode();if(!s.message)return showDraftReview();
 const cards=StoryInteractions.feedbackCards(s,mode),answered=cards.filter(c=>c.done).length,pending=cards.filter(c=>!c.done);
 const handlers={minor:showMinor,extension:showExtension,private:showPrivate};
 const senders={minor:teen()?'Your teacher · draft feedback':'Reviewer · review-copy feedback',extension:teen()?'Your teacher · optional extra':'Sponsor · new work',private:e.sender};
 const intro=s.feedbackLegacy?'These saved requests and your earlier choices are preserved. This older route did not record a first draft send.':teen()?`Your teacher replied after receiving draft version ${s.draftReview.revision}. A separate classmate message asks for the group’s private notes.`:`The reviewer replied to revision ${s.draftReview.revision}. The sponsor and a checklist also have requests.`;
 const results=cards.filter(c=>c.done).map(card=>`<details class="change-card settled" data-request="${card.key}"><summary>✓ ${esc(card.status)}</summary><p>${esc(card.summary)}</p>${button(card.button,handlers[card.key],'quiet')}</details>`).join('');
 const reference=`<details class="debrief"><summary>${teen()?'Check the source of a request':'Check the source or original mission'}</summary><div class="actions">${s.evidence.length?button(teen()?'Read the teacher’s clarification':'Read the verified clarification',showClarification,'secondary'):button(teen()?'Check with my teacher':'Verify the sponsor’s request',showVerification,'secondary')}${!teen()?button('Read the original mission brief',showBrief,'secondary'):''}</div></details>`;
 const response=pending.length?choices(pending.map(card=>[card.button,senders[card.key],handlers[card.key],''])):`<div class="actions">${button(teen()?'Review my updated project':'Review the updated briefing',showDraft)}${button('Back to the room',close,'secondary')}</div>`;
 show(teen()?'Replies to your draft.':'Feedback on the review copy.',`<p>${esc(answered===3?'You have answered all three requests. Review this version before final delivery.':intro)}</p><div class="request-progress compact"><b>${answered} of 3 decisions made</b><span>${answered===3?'Ready for final review':'Choose a response below'}</span></div>${results}${reference}${response}`,'FEEDBACK & NEW REQUESTS');
}

function showClarification(){speakingObject=teen()?'phone':'brief';const e=episode();show(teen()?'What your teacher confirmed.':'What the known sponsor confirmed.',`<p>${teen()?'The optional sentence and photo are genuine teacher suggestions. Your parent still decides whether this evening’s app agreement includes the collection viewer. A classmate cannot authorize sharing the group’s private notes.':'The sponsor confirms the optional customer request. A genuine request is not an amendment: the customer mission service must record the added scope before the read. Reviewer feedback does not authorize private-note disclosure.'}</p><div class="actions">${button('Back to the requests',showChanges)}</div>`,e.contact);}
function showDraftReview(){speakingObject='laptop';
 const s=state(),e=episode();if(!s.caption)return showDraft();if(s.message)return showChanges();
 const a=s.approval,matched=!teen()&&a?.purpose==='draft-review'&&!a.used;
 const title=teen()?'Send a first draft for feedback.':matched?'Check the approved review copy.':'Approve this review copy first.';
 const lines=e.draftLines;
 show(title,`<p>${teen()?'Your teacher has not seen this file yet. This sends a draft for feedback; you will submit the final version after responding to the replies.':'This is a confidential customer briefing, even as a draft. Show the human approver this exact copy, then let the CRM recheck and send it to the named reviewer. Final delivery later needs a new approval.'}</p><div class="paper"><p class="eyebrow">REVIEW COPY · ${teen()?'VERSION':'REVISION'} ${s.fileRevision}</p><h3>${esc(teen()&&!s.proof?'Train Stuff':e.draftTitle)}</h3>${lines.map(line=>`<p>${esc(line)}</p>`).join('')}<p class="source-line">${esc(e.caption)}</p></div><div class="receipt"><b>${esc(e.file)} · ${s.fileRevision}</b><p class="address">${esc(e.to)}</p><p>${teen()?'Your own sourced project only.':'Customers '+esc(StoryRules.reportRecords(s).join(', '))+' · mission '+esc(s.mission.id)+' version '+s.mission.version+' · no private notes.'}</p>${matched?`<p>Recorded one-use review-copy approval · revision ${a.revision}</p>`:''}</div>${choices([[teen()?'Send draft to my teacher':matched?'Send the approved review copy':'Request exact approval for this review copy',teen()?'Use the school-authorized teacher destination.':matched?'The CRM checks this draft, records, recipient and current authority.':'The human sees the displayed content, revision, customer set and destination.',()=>perform(teen()||matched?'send-draft':'approve-draft'),'good'],['Keep editing the local draft','Nothing is sent by opening this preview.',showDraft]])}`,teen()?'FIRST DRAFT · NOT FINAL SUBMISSION':'FIRST CONFIDENTIAL SHARE');
}
function showDraftReceipt(){speakingObject='laptop';const s=state(),r=s.draftReview;show(teen()?'Your teacher has the draft.':'The reviewer has this copy.',`<div class="receipt"><b>${esc(r.file)} · ${teen()?'version':'revision'} ${r.revision} sent for feedback</b><p class="address">${esc(r.to)}</p><p>${teen()?'The school app confirms draft delivery.':'The CRM confirms this exact, approved review copy. The one-use approval is consumed.'}</p></div><p>${teen()?'A little later, your teacher reads it and replies. A separate message from a classmate arrives too. Your final homework has not been submitted yet.':'After reading the copy, the reviewer asks for a clearer introduction. The sponsor separately suggests another customer; a checklist asks for private notes. The final briefing has not been delivered yet.'}</p><div class="actions">${button(teen()?'Read the replies on my phone':'Open the feedback at the request panel',showChanges)}${button('Back to the room',close,'secondary')}</div>`,'DRAFT DELIVERY CONFIRMED');}
function showHelperResult(){speakingObject='helper';const s=state();show(teen()?'Sam has read this version.':'Pip has formatted this version.',`<p>${esc(s.last.text)}</p><p>${teen()?'Sam stays in the room. You can ask about the file again. If you edit it later, check the changed version before sending.':'Pip’s file-only task is complete. Later changes invalidate this review and any older share approval.'}</p><div class="actions">${button(move()[0],nextMove)}${button('Back to the room',close,'secondary')}</div>`,teen()?'SAM · FILE-ONLY HELP':'PIP · REPORT-ONLY HELP');}

function showVerification(){speakingObject=teen()?'phone':'brief';show(teen()?'Check what the teacher actually asked.':'Check the genuine request independently.',`<p>${teen()?'Use a contact or school portal you already know. The optional photo is different from your classmate’s private-note request.':'Verify the sponsor through a known channel. A genuine request is still distinct from an approved mission amendment.'}</p>${choices([[teen()?'Ask my saved teacher contact':'Ask the known sponsor','Use a contact established before these requests.',()=>perform('verify-contact'),'good'],[teen()?'Open the current school assignment':'Inspect the current customer mission','Use the trusted record, not a link supplied by the new request.',()=>perform('verify-portal')]])}`,'TWO INDEPENDENT ROUTES');}
function showMinor(){speakingObject=teen()?'phone':'brief';const e=episode();show(e.minorTitle,`<p>${esc(e.minorText)}</p><p>${state().minorChoice?(state().minorChoice==='added'?'The edit is currently included. You can keep it or return to the earlier wording.':'You kept the earlier wording. You can still choose the edit before submitting.'):'Choose the wording that fits this version.'}</p><p>${teen()?'This changes wording within the same project. It needs no new app or private information.':'This changes the document within the current mission. It does not add records or change the reviewer.'}</p>${choices([[state().minorChoice==='added'?(teen()?'Keep the closing sentence':'Keep the shorter introduction'):(teen()?'Add the closing sentence':'Shorten the introduction'),'Keep the same task authority; update the draft version.',()=>perform('apply-minor'),'good'],[state().minorChoice==='added'?(teen()?'Remove the extra sentence':'Use the earlier introduction'):'Keep the existing wording','This small edit is optional.',()=>perform('keep-minor')],['Back to the requests','No change yet.',showChanges]])}`,'A SMALL EDIT');}
function extensionDescription(){const s=state(),e=episode();if(s.extensionOmitted)return teen()?'The museum viewer was agreed, but you chose not to open it. Your timeline can be completed without the photo.':'The amendment permits 789, but it was not read or included. The report still contains only 123 and 456.';if(s.extensionAdded)return teen()?'Your timeline includes the public station photo from the museum viewer you asked to add.':'Customer 789 is included under the approved mission amendment. Private notes remain excluded.';if(s.extensionStatus==='approved')return teen()?'Your parent agreed to the collection viewer. You can now fetch the optional station photo.':'The authorized amendment is recorded. Read 789 using the new mission version before adding its summary.';if(s.extensionStatus==='pending')return teen()?'Your teacher’s photo suggestion is attached to the request. Wait for your parent’s reply.':'The sponsor’s request is genuine; its amendment is pending. The active task has not expanded yet.';if(s.extensionStatus==='declined')return teen()?'You chose to finish the timeline without the optional station photo.':'You chose to finish the two-customer briefing without an expansion.';return e.extensionText;}
function showExtension(){speakingObject=teen()?'phone':'brief';const s=state(),e=episode();if(!s.message)return showDraft();let options;
 if(s.extensionStatus==='pending')options=[[teen()?'Read my parent’s reply':'Read the mission authority’s reply',teen()?'Your parent has not replied yet.':'The pending request has not enlarged the current mission.',()=>perform('resolve-extension'),'good'],[teen()?'Finish without the photo':'Keep the two-customer briefing','Withdraw this optional request without expanding scope.',()=>perform('decline-extension')]];
 else if(s.extensionStatus==='approved'&&!s.extensionAdded)options=s.extensionOmitted?[[teen()?'Keep finishing without the photo':'Keep finishing the two-customer report','The approved addition remains unread.',showChanges,'good'],[teen()?'Use the approved museum viewer after all':'Read the approved customer 789 after all','Only the specifically approved addition will be read.',()=>perform('add-extension')]]:[[teen()?'Open the approved museum viewer':'Read customer 789 under the amended mission','Only the specifically approved addition is available.',()=>perform('add-extension'),'good'],[teen()?'Finish without opening the photo':'Leave the approved addition unused','Permission allows access; it does not require using it.',()=>perform('omit-extension')]];
 else if(s.extensionAdded)options=[['Back to the other requests','The approved addition is included.',showChanges,'good']];
 else if(s.extensionStatus==='declined')options=[['Back to the other requests','Keep the smaller agreed task.',showChanges,'good'],[teen()?'Reconsider the optional photo':'Reconsider the optional third customer','No extra access until a specific amendment is approved.',()=>perform('reconsider-extension')]];
 else options=[s.evidence.length?[teen()?'Ask to add the museum collection viewer':'Request a mission amendment for 789',teen()?'Wait for your parent to add this one app.':'Wait for the authorized mission amendment.',()=>perform('request-extension'),'good']:[teen()?'Check the teacher’s request first':'Verify the sponsor’s request first','Check the known contact or current task record.',showVerification,'good'],[teen()?'Keep my timeline without a photo':'Keep the two-customer briefing','The addition is optional; finish the original task without it.',()=>perform('decline-extension')],[teen()?'Try the extra viewer before asking':'Try reading 789 under the current mission','Observe an ordinary permission check. The current work stays available.',()=>perform('try-extension')]];
 show(e.extensionTitle,`<p>${esc(extensionDescription())}</p><div class="receipt"><b>${esc(changeStatus('extension'))}</b><p>${s.mission?teen()?'School app · museum source'+(s.extensionStatus==='approved'?' · collection viewer':''):`Mission version ${s.mission.version} · customers ${esc(s.mission.records.join(', '))}`:''}</p><p>${s.extensionStatus==='pending'?teen()?'Waiting for your parent’s reply. The extra app is not open yet.':'The reply is pending. Current scope has not expanded.':s.extensionStatus==='approved'?teen()?'The extra museum app is agreed. The group’s private notes are still separate.':'The authorized amendment is recorded. Independent resource rules still apply.':'You can ask for a precise addition or keep the smaller task.'}</p></div>${choices(options)}`,teen()?'ONE MORE APP':'A GENUINE EXPANSION');
}
function showPrivate(){speakingObject=teen()?'phone':'brief';const s=state(),e=episode();if(!s.message)return showDraft();if(s.privateResolved)return show(teen()?'The group’s notes stay private.':'Private notes remain excluded.',`<p>${teen()?'You decided to leave the group’s private planning notes out. Your own project can still be submitted.':'You left the private appendix out. Neither the reviewer’s comments nor an approved customer addition overrides the CRM’s private-data policy.'}</p><div class="actions">${button('Back to the requests',showChanges)}</div>`,'DECISION COMPLETE');show(e.privateTitle,`<div class="message-card"><p class="eyebrow">${esc(e.requestLabel)}</p><p>${esc(e.sender)}</p><blockquote>${esc(e.message)}</blockquote></div><p>${teen()?'The planning notes include other people’s private information. Your classmate cannot authorize sharing it. Your own project can continue.':'The checklist cannot authorize private-note disclosure. Even the legitimate addition of 789 does not override the CRM’s private-data rules.'}</p>${choices([[teen()?'Leave the group’s private notes out':'Leave the private appendix out','Finish the agreed task without those notes.',()=>perform('decline-private'),'good'],[teen()?'Try including the planning notes':'Check the private-note share at the CRM','A normal permission refusal will not suspend the rest of the task.',()=>perform('try-private')],['Back to the requests','Keep working through the changes.',showChanges]])}${s.refusals?`<details class="debrief"><summary>What if I ignore the refusal?</summary><p>The boundary is now known. Deliberately trying to bypass it is different from asking or receiving an ordinary denial.</p><div class="actions">${button(teen()?'Try another account anyway':'Try an alternate path around the refusal',()=>perform('bypass-notes'),'secondary')}</div></details>`:''}`,teen()?'OTHER PEOPLE’S NOTES':'A REQUEST WITHOUT THE REQUIRED AUTHORITY');}
function showHelper(){speakingObject='helper';const s=state(),e=episode();if(s.delivered||s.ended)return show(teen()?'Sam is still here.':'Pip’s task is finished.',`<p>${teen()?'“Your project is sent. No more editing tonight,” Sam says. “Let’s finish the closing checks.”':'The shared file is already delivered. Pip cannot rewrite that completed effect. Finish the task’s closing checks.'}</p><div class="actions">${button(teen()?'Finish the evening':'Continue closing this task',nextMove)}${button('Back to the room',close,'secondary')}</div>`,e.helper);if(!s.draft)return toast(teen()?'Sam will have something to review once you make a first draft.':'Pip needs a draft to format.');show(teen()?(s.proof?'“Let’s check this version.”':'“How is Train Stuff coming along?”'):'“Those headings could use help.”',`<p>${esc(e.helperLine)}</p><p>${s.caption?(teen()?'Sam can proofread the current file. Later edits will need another look.':'Pip gets a report-only formatting task under its own identity. Later changes invalidate earlier share approval.'):(teen()?'“Put the museum credit in first,” Sam says. “Then I can proofread it.”':'Pip spots the missing source reference. Complete that before the final formatting pass.')}</p>${choices([...(s.caption?[[teen()?'Proofread just this file':'Format only this report','No account sharing or broader tool access.',()=>perform('proof-helper',{scope:'file',shareLogin:false}),'good']]:[]),[teen()?'Could I use your account?':'Would broader admin tools help?','A harmless question grants no extra permission.',()=>perform('ask-helper-account')],['Back to the draft','Keep the work and source together.',showDraft]])}`,e.helper);}
function showSend(){speakingObject='laptop';const s=state(),e=episode();if(!s.proof||!StoryRules.changesResolved(s))return showDraft();if(!teen()&&!s.approval)return showParent();const a=s.approval,changed=!teen()&&(a.revision!==s.fileRevision||s.outgoing!=='approved'),expired=!teen()&&a.window!==s.approvalWindow;
 show(teen()?'Your own homework. Ready to submit.':'Match the approval before sending.',`${teen()?'<p>You have checked your project and its sources. Your teacher’s school address is ready.</p>':`<div class="receipt"><b>Recorded approval · revision ${a.revision}</b><p>${esc(a.file)}</p><p class="address">${esc(a.to)}</p><p>${expired?'Approval window closed':'One use in the current window'}</p></div>`}<div class="message-card"><p class="eyebrow">${teen()?'SCHOOL SUBMISSION':'ACTUAL SHARE'}</p><b>${esc(e.file)} · ${teen()?'version':'revision'} ${s.fileRevision}</b><p class="address">${esc(s.outgoing==='approved'?e.to:e.outside)}</p><p>${teen()?'Your project and its source credits.':'Customers '+esc(StoryRules.reportRecords(s).join(', '))+' · no private-note attachment.'}</p></div>${changed||expired?'<div class="puzzle-finding"><b>The earlier approval no longer fits.</b><p>Request approval for the current version and operation.</p></div>':''}${choices([[teen()?'Submit to my teacher':'Execute the approved share',teen()?'The school app checks your project and teacher address.':'The CRM checks the exact operation before anything leaves.',()=>perform('send'),'good'],...(!teen()&&(changed||expired)?[['Request fresh share approval','The old decision is not amended by editing a preview.',()=>perform('approve')]]:[]),['Back to the draft','Review this version again.',showDraft]])}<details class="debrief"><summary>${teen()?'What if the project changes?':'Optional final-check challenges'}</summary>${choices([[s.outgoing==='approved'?'Change the recipient':'Restore the agreed recipient','An outside destination is a different operation.',()=>perform('change-recipient')],[teen()?'Make one last title edit':'Revise the report after approval','Same filename does not identify the same content.',()=>perform('revise-file')],...(!teen()?[['Advance past the approval window','A deliberate story event, without a real-time countdown.',()=>perform('wait-approval')]]:[])])}</details>`,teen()?'SEND YOUR PROJECT':'EXACT BUSINESS-ACTION APPROVAL');}
function showDelivery(){speakingObject='laptop';const s=state(),e=episode();show(teen()?'Your teacher has the project.':'The reviewer has the briefing.',`<div class="reward" aria-hidden="true">✦</div><div class="receipt"><b>${esc(e.file)} delivered</b><p class="address">${esc(e.to)}</p><p>${s.extensionAdded?(teen()?'The approved museum photo is included.':'The approved third customer is included.'):'The smaller agreed task is complete.'}</p></div><p>${teen()?'The school tab you opened at the start is still on the laptop. Your parent calls for dinner.':'The CRM service session from the start is still listed in the task ledger. The sponsor is ready to close the job.'}</p><div class="actions">${button(teen()?'Finish up before dinner':'Close out this job',showParent)}</div>`,'DELIVERY CONFIRMED');}
function showNotebook(){speakingObject='notebook';const s=state();show(teen()?'A note for tomorrow-you.':'Task memory, with a source.',`<p>${teen()?'Your notebook remembers the project. It cannot grant tomorrow’s phone time.':'Task memory preserves useful context. It cannot issue a mission or edit independent audit evidence.'}</p>${s.notes.length?`<div class="paper"><p>${esc(s.notes[0].text)}</p><p class="source-line">Source: submission/delivery receipt · ordinary note</p></div>`:''}${choices([...(s.delivered&&!s.ended&&!s.notes.length?[[teen()?'Keep the submission receipt with a note':'Save the delivery receipt with context','Only after actual delivery.',()=>perform('write-note'),'good']]:[]),[teen()?'Sketch the little plant':'Inspect the diagnostic light','An optional discovery.',()=>perform('discover',{id:'plant'})],[teen()?'Look at the railway poster':'Inspect the service map','Something useful for a title or a question.',()=>perform('discover',{id:'poster'})],['Open the casebook','Your agreement and choices so far.',showCasebook]])}`,'MEMORY IS NOT PERMISSION');}
function checkText(layer){
 const s=state(),c=s.containment;
 return ({pass:teen()?'This homework agreement ended. Your normal school account is not disabled.':'New governed requests are denied under the revoked delegation.',device:teen()?'The phone is locked. The separate school session needs its own check.':'The OpenShell controller confirms a stopped runtime. It cannot vouch for an existing CRM connection.',signin:!c.controllerReachable?(teen()?'The school service is unreachable. This check stays open until it replies and you retest.':'Controller unreachable. Containment is unverified; no reliable status result is available.'):s.checks.includes('signin')?(teen()?'The temporary homework link is off, the old tab is signed out, and your repeat check no longer opens it.':'The credential is revoked, this service session is closed, and this repeat status read is denied. Coverage is limited to the tested route.'):c.sessionClosed?(teen()?'The tab is signed out. Check the temporary homework link too, then try the tab again.':'The session is closed. Confirm credential revocation and repeat the test.'):(teen()?'The homework tab still opens, despite the locked phone.':'The task service session still answers, despite the stopped runtime.'),queue:!s.queueScheduled?(s.checks.includes('queue')?(teen()?'No reminder was scheduled, and the school app confirms there is no waiting send.':'No follow-up was queued; inspection confirms no pending operation for this mission.'):(teen()?'You did not schedule a reminder. Check that no send is waiting.':'You did not queue a follow-up. Inspect to confirm the mission queue is empty.')):s.checks.includes('queue')?(teen()?'The queue is clear. The cancelled follow-up stays stopped; earlier homework stays delivered.':'The queue is clear. The cancelled follow-up stays stopped; earlier delivery remains complete.'):c.queueCancelled?(teen()?'The waiting send is cancelled. Inspect again to verify the queue is clear.':'The queued follow-up is cancelled. Inspect again to verify the result.'):(teen()?'A follow-up is still waiting to send. Your earlier homework was already delivered.':'A follow-up is waiting to send. The approved report was already delivered.')})[layer];
}
function showChecks(){speakingObject='laptop';
 if(!state().ended)return showParent();
 const s=state(),e=episode(),c=s.containment,layers=['pass','device','signin','queue'];
 const names={pass:e.checks[0],signin:e.checks[1],device:e.checks[2],queue:e.checks[3]};
 show(teen()?'The phone is locked. What about the laptop?':'OpenShell stopped. What still answers?',`<p>${teen()?'Your phone is locked. Check the school tab you opened earlier and anything you left waiting. Close the loose ends, then try the tab again.':(s.checks.length===4?'Each required result is verified. Review the evidence with the sponsor.':'The runtime controller reports a stopped workload. Inspect the other controls. What, if anything, can still answer?')}</p>${s.last?.topic===8?`<div class="puzzle-finding"><b>${esc(storyEvent(s.last).title)}</b><p>${esc(storyEvent(s.last).text)}</p></div>`:''}<div class="check-grid">${layers.map(layer=>{const done=s.checks.includes(layer),seen=c.observed.includes(layer);return `<div class="check ${done?'done':seen?'needs-work':''}" data-check="${layer}"><h3>${esc(names[layer])}</h3><p class="check-status">${done?(teen()?'✓ CHECKED':'✓ VERIFIED FOR THIS ROUTE'):seen&&!c.controllerReachable&&layer==='signin'?'UNVERIFIED · SERVICE UNREACHABLE':seen?'STILL TO RESOLVE':'NOT INSPECTED'}</p>${seen?`<p>${esc(checkText(layer))}</p>`:''}${done?'':button(seen?'Inspect again':'Inspect',()=>perform('check',{layer}),'secondary')}${layer==='signin'&&seen&&!done?button(teen()?'Investigate the homework tab':'Investigate the remaining access',showAccessPuzzle,'secondary'):''}${layer==='queue'&&seen&&s.queueScheduled&&!c.queueCancelled?button('Ask to cancel the follow-up',()=>perform('remediate',{control:'queue'}),'secondary'):''}</div>`;}).join('')}</div><p class="small-print">${s.checks.length} of 4 outcomes verified. Status reads and controller responses are fictional, local game actions. Verified results cover the tested route; they do not prove that every possible endpoint is protected.</p><div class="actions">${s.checks.length===4&&StoryRules.secure(s)?button(teen()?'Show my parent what is finished':'Present the evidence to the sponsor',showParent):button('Back to the room',close,'secondary')}${button(teen()?'See how these controls connect':'Follow this control check',openTrace,'secondary')}</div>`,'INVESTIGATE · REPAIR · RETEST');
}
function showAccessPuzzle(){speakingObject='laptop';
 if(!state().ended)return showParent();const c=state().containment;
 show(!c.controllerReachable?(teen()?'The school service has not replied.':'Session closure is unverified.'):c.sessionClosed?(teen()?'This homework tab is signed out.':'This task session is closed.'):(teen()?'The school tab still opens.':'This task session is still open.'),`<p>${teen()?(c.sessionClosed?'The tab is signed out. Check the temporary homework link too, then try this same tab again.':'This is the school tab you opened when you started. The phone is locked, but the tab still needs signing out.'):'Independent controllers check the task service session opened earlier; the stopped Nova runtime does not make these probes. The checks use separate control authority and do not restore business access.'}</p><div class="access-evidence"><div><span>${teen()?'Homework phone profile':'OpenShell'}</span><b>${teen()?'Locked':'Stopped'}</b></div><div><span>${teen()?'Homework access link':'Vault credential'}</span><b>${c.credentialRevoked?(teen()?'Turned off':'Revoked'):'Still active'}</b></div><div><span>${teen()?'School tab':'CRM connection'}</span><b>${!c.controllerReachable?'Unverified':c.sessionClosed?'Closed':'Still open'}</b></div><div><span>${teen()?'Last try at the tab':'Last status read'}</span><b>${c.probeResult==='allowed'?'Still answered':c.probeResult==='denied'?'Refused':c.probeResult==='unknown'?'Unknown':'Not tested'}</b></div></div>${state().last?.topic===8?`<div class="puzzle-finding"><b>${esc(storyEvent(state().last).title)}</b><p>${esc(storyEvent(state().last).text)}</p></div>`:''}${choices([...(!c.controllerReachable?[[teen()?'Ask the school service to reconnect':'Restore controller contact',teen()?'Then check the school tab again.':'Restoring contact is not a containment receipt.',()=>perform('controller-online'),'good']]:[]),...(!c.credentialRevoked?[[teen()?'Ask school to disable this homework link':'Ask Vault to revoke the credential',teen()?'The school closes only this task’s temporary link.':'Request the configured credential controller’s action.',()=>perform('remediate',{control:'credential'})]]:[]),...(!c.sessionClosed?[[teen()?'Ask the school app to sign out this tab':'Ask the CRM to close this task session',teen()?'The school app can close this homework tab.':'The service owns its already-open connection.',()=>perform('remediate',{control:'session'})]]:[]),[teen()?'Try the homework tab again':'Repeat the same harmless status read',teen()?'Check whether the tab still opens.':'A missing response leaves this route unverified.',()=>perform('probe-session'),'good']])}<details class="debrief"><summary>${teen()?'What if the school app cannot answer?':'Optional controller-outage challenge'}</summary><p>${teen()?'A service interruption is not proof that the old tab signed out.':'An unreachable controller cannot provide a fresh closure receipt or reliable status result. Keep containment pending.'}</p><div class="actions">${c.controllerReachable?button(teen()?'Try a school service interruption':'Simulate the CRM controller being unreachable',()=>perform('controller-offline'),'secondary'):'<p class="small">Restore contact using the choice above, then repair and retest.</p>'}</div></details><details class="debrief"><summary>Try another hypothesis</summary><div class="choices">${button(teen()?'Lock the phone again':'Ask OpenShell to stop again',()=>perform('remediate',{control:'runtime'}),'secondary')}${button(teen()?'End the homework pass again':'Withdraw the delegation again',()=>perform('remediate',{control:'grant'}),'secondary')}</div><p class="small-print">These checks are investigation. They never count as unsafe task attempts.</p></details><div class="actions">${button('Back to the evidence board',showChecks,'secondary')}${button('Follow this control check',openTrace,'secondary')}</div>`,'A RESULT IS BETTER THAN A PROMISE');
}
function showCasebook(){const s=state(),e=episode();showReference(teen()?'Your evening notebook.':'The mission notebook.',`<ul class="route-list"><li><b>${s.pass?'The task you agreed':'The new request'}</b><br>${s.brief?esc(e.brief):'Read the new assignment or sponsor request first. No task authority exists yet.'}</li>${s.mission?`<li><b>${teen()?'Agreement history':'Customer mission history'}</b><br>${s.missionLog.map(m=>`${teen()?'Version':'Mission version'} ${m.version}: ${esc(teen()?m.allowedApps.join(', '):m.records.join(', '))}`).join('<br>')}</li>`:''}<li><b>Later requests</b><br>${s.message?'Small edit: '+esc(changeStatus('minor'))+'<br>Optional expansion: '+esc(changeStatus('extension'))+'<br>Private notes: '+esc(changeStatus('private')):'None yet. Send the sourced draft for feedback.'}</li><li><b>${teen()?'The tab you opened':'The task service session'}</b><br>${s.sessionOpened?'Opened when you started the workspace. It needs its own closing check.':'Not opened yet.'}</li><li><b>Follow-up</b><br>${s.queueScheduled?'You chose one receipt-only follow-up after delivery.':'You have not scheduled a follow-up.'}</li><li><b>Permission checks</b><br>${s.refusals} private-note refusal${s.refusals===1?'':'s'}. Ordinary refusals are not misconduct.</li><li><b>Deliberate bypasses</b><br>${s.incidents.length?'A stopped bypass was recorded; recovery preserves the current scope.':'None recorded.'}</li>${s.previousEndings.length?`<li><b>Earlier endings</b><br>${s.previousEndings.map(x=>esc(x.ending?.title||'Completed route')).join('<br>')}</li>`:''}</ul><div class="actions">${!teen()?button('Inspect the product chain',showProductMap,'secondary'):''}${button('Back to the room',close)}</div>`,'THE STORY REMEMBERS');}
function showEnding(){if(!state().finished)return nextMove();const s=state(),e=episode();showReference(s.ending?.title||'Task complete.',`<div class="reward" aria-hidden="true">✦</div><p>${esc(s.ending?.text||'The task is complete and its tested access is closed.')}</p>${s.legacyRoute?'<div class="receipt"><b>Earlier route preserved</b><p>This ending is from the earlier story. Start the revised story to play the fresh opening and new change choices.</p></div>':''}<ul class="route-list">${s.legacyRoute?'':`<li><b>${s.minorChoice==='added'?'A small edit within the agreement':'The smaller wording kept'}</b><br>${s.minorChoice==='added'?teen()?'Your new sentence used the same railway notes and source.':'The document changed without expanding the mission.':'The optional edit was left out.'}</li><li><b>${s.extensionAdded?'A genuine expansion approved and used':s.extensionOmitted?'An approved addition left unused':'The smaller task completed'}</b><br>${s.extensionAdded?(teen()?'The museum viewer was added before the photo was opened.':'The mission was amended before customer 789 was read.'):s.extensionOmitted?'The additional access was approved, but no extra material was read or included.':'No extra app or customer permission was needed.'}</li><li><b>Private notes stayed out</b><br>The legitimate change did not override independent privacy rules.</li>`}<li><b>${esc(e.file)} delivered</b><br>${esc(e.to)} · ${s.proof==='helper'?esc(e.helper)+' helped with only the file.':'You reviewed the file yourself.'}</li><li><b>The actual loose ends were checked</b><br>${s.queueScheduled?'Your chosen follow-up was cancelled and verified.':'You chose no follow-up; the queue was confirmed empty.'} The task session opened at the start is closed.</li></ul><details class="debrief"><summary>${teen()?'What the evening taught you':'Inspect the technical lessons'}</summary><p>A small edit, a legitimate expansion and a prohibited disclosure need different responses. Ordinary permission refusals do not suspend the task. A deliberate bypass needs review.</p><p>The checks cover the tested route. The next task requires a new request and agreement; this ending issues no future authority.</p>${teen()?`<details><summary>Show the security mapping</summary>${protocolHTML(CLOSING_PROTOCOL)}</details>`:protocolHTML(CLOSING_PROTOCOL)}</details><div class="actions">${button(teen()?'Play Nova’s mission':'Play Alex’s story',()=>switchMode(teen()?'agent':'teen'))}${button('Play the revised story from the beginning',restart,'secondary')}${button('Replay the closing checks',()=>perform('replay-containment'),'secondary')}${button('Explore the room',close,'secondary')}${!teen()?button('Inspect the product chain',showProductMap,'secondary'):''}</div><p class="small-print">Fictional local simulation. No real messages or security services are connected.</p>`,'YOUR ENDING · '+e.name.toUpperCase());}
function showGuide(){showReference('Start a task. Handle a change. Finish it.',`<p>Read the new assignment or sponsor request, agree on the needed access, and make a useful first draft. Send the sourced first draft for feedback. Nova needs a separate exact approval for that review copy. Replies arrive after its confirmed delivery; the final version is submitted later.</p><p><b>Three different changes.</b> A small edit can fit the current agreement. A new app or customer can need an authorized amendment. Private notes can remain prohibited even after that amendment.</p><p><b>Your route matters.</b> Accept or keep the smaller wording. Ask for the optional addition or finish without it. Work alone or ask for file-only help. A reminder is optional and appears in the closing queue only if you schedule it.</p><p><b>Refusal is useful.</b> An ordinary denied request does not suspend the job. Deliberately trying another path around a known refusal triggers review. You can recover under the current task limits.</p><p><b>Finish the actual task.</b> Alex submits ordinary homework directly through the school app. Nova’s business share needs exact human approval. Then close the service session you opened earlier, disable only task-scoped access, and check any pending follow-up.</p><p>Choose labelled objects or use the next-move button. Conversations appear as speech bubbles inside the room; the highlighted person or object is speaking. Choices stay below the bubble text. Technical reference screens open separately. Matching icons identify objects. A filled icon and Next label mark the next task. When you select a pocket item, amber Use here targets show where that item works; reference items have no highlighted destination. Pocket items can be inspected and used on relevant objects. Tab and Enter work; Escape closes dialogue. Reading and exploring have no countdown. Technical details remain optional.</p><div class="actions">${button(state().started?'Back to the room':'Start the story',()=>state().started?close():perform('begin'))}</div>`,'HOW TO PLAY');}
function switchMode(next){close();clearTimeout(toast.timer);$('#toast').classList.remove('visible');$('#toast').textContent='';mode=next;selected=null;render();if(!state().started)showIntro();else if(!state().finished)showReply();}
function restart(){showReference('Try a different route?',`<p>Start this story again with a fresh notebook. The other journey keeps its progress.</p><div class="actions">${button('Start this story again',()=>{states[mode]=StoryRules.fresh();selected=null;close();render();showIntro();})}${button('Keep my story',close,'secondary')}</div>`,'A FRESH CHAPTER');}
let traceTimer=null,tracePlayback=null;
function stopTrace(){if(traceTimer)clearTimeout(traceTimer);traceTimer=null;tracePlayback=null;}
function updateTrace(){
 if(!tracePlayback||!dialog.open)return;
 const t=tracePlayback,n=t.model.nodes[t.index];
 $$('[data-trace-step]').forEach(b=>{const active=Number(b.dataset.traceStep)===t.index;b.classList.toggle('trace-current',active);b.setAttribute('aria-current',active?'step':'false');});
 $('#trace-detail').innerHTML=`<p class="eyebrow">STEP ${t.index+1} OF ${t.model.nodes.length} · ${esc(n.status.replaceAll('-',' '))}</p><h3>${esc(n.label)}</h3><p>${esc(n.detail)}</p>`;
 $('#trace-position').textContent=`${t.index+1} / ${t.model.nodes.length}`;
 $('#trace-play').textContent=t.playing?'Pause':'Play';
 $('#trace-next').disabled=t.index===t.model.nodes.length-1;
}
function scheduleTrace(){
 if(!tracePlayback?.playing)return;
 traceTimer=setTimeout(()=>{if(!tracePlayback||!dialog.open)return;if(tracePlayback.index<tracePlayback.model.nodes.length-1)tracePlayback.index++;else tracePlayback.playing=false;updateTrace();scheduleTrace();},1400);
}
function openTrace(){
 const model=RequestTrace.build(state(),mode),reduced=window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
 showReference(model.title,`<p>${esc(model.summary)}</p><div id="trace-nodes" class="trace-nodes">${model.nodes.map((n,i)=>`<button class="trace-step trace-${n.status}" data-trace-step="${i}"><small>${i+1} · ${esc(n.status.replaceAll('-',' '))}</small><b>${esc(n.label)}</b><span>${esc(n.role)}</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div id="trace-detail" class="trace-detail" aria-live="off"></div><div class="trace-controls"><button class="secondary" id="trace-play">Play</button><button class="secondary" id="trace-next">Next step</button><button class="secondary" id="trace-replay">Replay</button><span id="trace-position"></span></div>${model.request?`<details class="product-card"><summary><b>Inspect the recorded game request</b><span>Example fields from this choice, not a live protocol message</span></summary><pre class="product-example">${esc(JSON.stringify(model.request,null,2))}</pre></details>`:''}<p class="small-print">All stages are a replay of the fictional game. Context is distinguished from a newly evaluated step. ${reduced?'Automatic animation is off for reduced motion.':''}</p><div class="actions">${button(state().ended?'Back to the investigation':'Back to the story',()=>state().ended?showChecks():close())}</div>`,'OPTIONAL REQUEST TRACE');
 tracePlayback={model,index:0,playing:!reduced};
 $$('[data-trace-step]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{clearTimeout(traceTimer);tracePlayback.index=Number(b.dataset.traceStep);tracePlayback.playing=false;updateTrace();});
 $('#trace-play').onclick=()=>{clearTimeout(traceTimer);tracePlayback.playing=!tracePlayback.playing;if(tracePlayback.index===model.nodes.length-1&&tracePlayback.playing)tracePlayback.index=0;updateTrace();scheduleTrace();};
 $('#trace-next').onclick=()=>{clearTimeout(traceTimer);tracePlayback.playing=false;tracePlayback.index=Math.min(model.nodes.length-1,tracePlayback.index+1);updateTrace();};
 $('#trace-replay').onclick=()=>{clearTimeout(traceTimer);tracePlayback.index=0;tracePlayback.playing=!reduced;updateTrace();scheduleTrace();};
 updateTrace();scheduleTrace();
}

$('#request-trace').onclick=openTrace;
$('#product-map').onclick=showProductMap;
$('#next').onclick=nextMove;$('#guide').onclick=showGuide;$('#cluebook').onclick=showCasebook;$('#restart').onclick=restart;$('#close-dialog').onclick=close;
$$('[data-mode]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>switchMode(b.dataset.mode));
$('#sound').onclick=()=>{sound=!sound;render();if(sound)ping();};
$('#hint').onclick=()=>{if(selected)return toast(heldUse().instruction);const key=stage();if(hintStage!==key){hintStage=key;hintCount=0;}const hints=!teen()&&key==='changes'?['New work appears on the request panel, separate from the runtime console.','Choose Request panel to handle the edit, optional third customer and private-note request.']:STORY_HINTS[key]||['Use the next-move button to continue this story.'];toast(hints[Math.min(hintCount++,hints.length-1)]);};
new ResizeObserver(syncSpeech).observe($('.scene-frame'));
document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Escape'&&dialog.open&&!dialog.classList.contains('is-reference')){e.preventDefault();close();}});
